# Obfuscation related
app.*.map.json

# NOTE: android/app/google-services.json is deliberately NOT ignored here.
#
# It is client configuration, not a credential: the API key inside it ships in
# every APK and is protected by the package name, not by secrecy. CI needs the
# file to build, and the first church's copy is committed for the same reason.
#
# The Firebase file that IS a secret is the *service-account* key, which lives on
# the server as storage/service-account.json and can send pushes. That one must
# never be committed — and, for the same reason, adding a second Android app to
# an EXISTING Firebase project does not isolate it: FCM topics are scoped to the
# project, not the app, so both churches' phones would share topic "all". Each
# church needs its own Firebase project.

# Release signing. key.properties carries the keystore PASSWORD.
android/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/

# Android Studio will place build artifacts here
/android/app/debug
/android/app/profile
/android/app/release
